 "lines": [
  [
   "hook",
   "This eight-mile gap is all that keeps the Mediterranean Sea alive."
  ],
  [
   "tease",
   "Close it, and the whole sea starts to vanish. And that's not just a theory."
  ],
  [
   "why",
   "The sun takes more water from this sea than its rivers bring back."
  ],
  [
   "inflow",
   "Only the Atlantic, pouring in right here, keeps it full."
  ],
  [
   "dam",
   "So what if we dammed it? Every year, the water drops. Spain's beach bars? Now they're desert bars."
  ],
  [
   "twist",
   "But here's the twist: it already happened."
  ],
  [
   "dry",
   "About six million years ago, its link to the Atlantic closed, and the Mediterranean largely dried out."
  ],
  [
   "salt",
   "In places, the salt it left is more than three thousand feet thick under the seafloor."
  ],
  [
   "flood",
   "Then the Atlantic smashed back in. One study says it mostly refilled in under two years, rising over thirty feet a day."
  ],
  [
   "plan",
   "And in the 1920s, a German architect really planned this dam, to drop the sea by up to six hundred sixty feet.",
   "And in the nineteen twenties, a German architect really planned this dam, to drop the sea by up to six hundred sixty feet."
  ],
  [
   "end",
   "Would you build it? Follow for more map stories."
  ]
 ],
